{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/913294-new-requiem-books","id":913294,"title":"New requiem books?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-13T01:23:56-07:00","id":913294,"title":"New requiem books?","content":"Hi guys, mage storyteller here speaking- I've never really played a requiem or joined this beautiful world but I must say coming from werewolf forsaken and awakening that this blood and smoke edition of the game is really appealing to me. I wanted to ask u, are there other books apart from the core rulebook of the 2nd edition? I'm speaking strictly about 2nd edition books not first edition requiem (I already have those). If not, is there anything scheduled for the future?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T01:32:20-07:00","id":913298,"title":"","content":"Nothing is out yet, though Secrets of the Covenants and Thousand Years Of Night are both being worked on right now. Dark Eras also has a chapter about the Kindred of the Elizabethan period, and I believe the Dark Eras Companion will have a Vampire/Promethean crossover set suring the Black Death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T01:46:03-07:00","id":913302,"title":"","content":"Secrets of the Covenants is supposed to be near to release (maybe two, three weeks?) as it's in <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/each-project-is-a-snowflake-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\">Layout phase</a>. A Thousand Years of Night is still a bit far away, as still is in Redlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T04:19:05-07:00","id":913336,"title":"","content":"While there aren't any 2nd Edition books out at the moment, I recommend checking out the books mentioned in 2nd Edition Core. <br /> <br /> Damnation City is a fantastic book to read to get an eye for some of the ways Kindred set up power bases and Domains. <br /> <br /> Blood Sorcery: Sacraments &amp; Blasphemy poses a more Awakening style approach to Cruac and Theban Sorcery and introduces other neat tricks along with some fun antagonists. <br /> <br /> Danse Macabre is a great toolbox book and you'll see a lot of the ideas posed in that book actually make it into 2nd Edition Core, it also has a reimagining of the Covenants as world spanning Conspiracies, and introduces several other new Covenants for the more familiar local games.<br /> <br /> And finally while the Covenant books are hit or miss the Clan Books are nothing but great ideas for character and plots all posted as in game accounts from the many and varied Kindred of the different Clans. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T06:52:24-07:00","id":913362,"title":"","content":"Thanks guys for ur quick replies and info!! I'll check it out then","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T10:14:29-07:00","id":913480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/913294-new-requiem-books?p=913336#post913336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Damnation City</b></u> is a fantastic book to read to get an eye for some of the ways Kindred set up power bases and Domains.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Blood Sorcery: Sacraments &amp; Blasphemy</b></u> poses a more Awakening style approach to Cruac and Theban Sorcery and introduces other neat tricks along with some fun antagonists.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Clan Books</b></u> are nothing but great ideas for character and plots all posted as in game accounts from the many and varied Kindred of the different Clans. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>So much this! As a Mage Storyteller Blood Sorcery will pique your interest; but the Clan Books and Damnation City are pure, non diluted, golden stuff for vampire.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T13:29:47-07:00","id":913627,"title":"","content":"Oh, before I forget. Another good series of books is the Bloodline Books.<br /> <br /> Even if you use none of the Bloodlines in your game the examples they give are fantastic for both story fodder and examples of what you can do with each of the five Clans. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}